  "source": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n  <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n  <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1\" />\n  <title>Comparison Landing</title>\n  <script type=\"application/json\" id=\"effect-meta\">\n  {\n    \"id\": \"template-comparison-landing\",\n    \"title\": \"Comparison Landing\",\n    \"summary\": \"A versus page with a verdict.\",\n    \"description\": \"A versus page with a verdict.\",\n    \"theme\": \"website-templates\",\n    \"categories\": [\"template\", \"page\"],\n    \"tags\": [\"template\", \"page\", \"comparison\", \"versus\", \"landing\", \"decision\"],\n    \"tech\": [\"css\"],\n    \"era\": \"2020s\",\n    \"difficulty\": \"advanced\",\n    \"dependencies\": [],\n    \"browser_support\": \"All modern browsers (Chromium, Firefox, Safari).\",\n    \"performance_notes\": \"Lightweight — composited transform/opacity work only.\",\n    \"accessibility_notes\": \"Full pages keep landmark elements (header, nav, main, footer), a single h1, and a visible focus order that matches the layout.\",\n    \"customization\": [\n      { \"name\": \"--c\", \"description\": \"Highlight\", \"default\": \"#7c5cff\" }\n    ],\n    \"variations\": [\"Reskin through the custom properties\", \"Swap the copy for your own\"],\n    \"ai_usage\": \"Comparison pages. State honestly where the alternative wins; a page where one side has no drawbacks reads as marketing and is discounted entirely.\"\n  }\n  </script>\n  <style>\n    *, *::before, *::after { box-sizing: border-box; }\n    html, body { margin: 0; }\n    body { background: #0b0d12; color: #e7ebf3;\n      font-family: system-ui, -apple-system, \"Segoe UI\", Roboto, sans-serif; }\n    body { padding: 1.4rem; max-width: 32rem; margin: 0 auto; }\n    h1 { margin: 0 0 .4rem; font-size: 1.5rem; }\n    .sub { margin: 0 0 1.2rem; color: #8b93a7; font-size: .88rem; line-height: 1.6; }\n    .cols { display: grid; grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr; gap: 10px; margin-bottom: 1.2rem; }\n    .col { padding: 1rem; border-radius: 14px; background: #151b2a; border: 1px solid #263149; }\n    .col.on { border-color: #7c5cff; }\n    .col b { font-size: .95rem; }\n    .col ul { margin: .5rem 0 0; padding-left: 1.1rem; color: #8b93a7; font-size: .8rem; line-height: 1.7; }\n    .verdict { padding: 1rem; border-radius: 14px; background: #191331; border: 1px solid #7c5cff; font-size: .86rem; line-height: 1.6; }\n    .verdict b { display: block; margin-bottom: .3rem; color: #b9a5ff; }\n  </style>\n</head>\n<body>\n  <h1>Catalogue vs. hand-rolled snippets</h1>\n  <p class=\"sub\">Both work. The difference is what happens after the first month.</p>\n  <div class=\"cols\"><div class=\"col on\"><b>Style Catalog</b><ul><li>One file per effect</li><li>Machine-readable metadata</li>\n  <li>Validated accessibility notes</li></ul></div>\n  <div class=\"col\"><b>Personal snippets</b><ul><li>Zero setup</li><li>Exactly your conventions</li><li>No search, no metadata</li></ul></div></div>\n  <div class=\"verdict\"><b>Verdict</b>Keep your snippets for one-offs. Use the catalogue when more than one person, or one agent, has to find the effect again.</div>\n</body>\n</html>\n"
